  <!-- HOW TO GET YOUR NIE -->
  <section class="msv__section">
    <div class="msv__container">
      <div class="msv__section-hd">
        <h2>How to Get Your NIE</h2>
        <p>Step-by-step process to obtain your NIE number</p>
      </div>
      <div class="msv__process-steps">
        <div class="msv__process-step">
          <div class="msv__process-step-num">1</div>
          <div class="msv__process-step-title">Prepare Documents</div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__process-step">
          <div class="msv__process-step-num">2</div>
          <div class="msv__process-step-title">Complete EX-15 Form</div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__process-step">
          <div class="msv__process-step-num">3</div>
          <div class="msv__process-step-title">Book Cita Previa</div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__process-step">
          <div class="msv__process-step-num">4</div>
          <div class="msv__process-step-title">Attend Appointment</div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__process-step">
          <div class="msv__process-step-num">5</div>
          <div class="msv__process-step-title">Pay Fee</div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__process-step">
          <div class="msv__process-step-num">6</div>
          <div class="msv__process-step-title">Receive NIE</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3>Detailed Steps</h3>
      <p><strong>Step 1: Gather Required Documents</strong></p>
      <p>Before you begin, ensure you have all necessary documents (see section below for full list).</p>

      <p><strong>Step 2: Complete the EX-15 Form</strong></p>
      <p>Fill out the official form EX-15 (available online on the National Police website or in person at the police station). You can complete it electronically or by hand. This form requests basic personal information, the reason for requesting the NIE, and your Spanish address (or address where you'll be contacted).</p>

      <p><strong>Step 3: Book Your Cita Previa (Appointment)</strong></p>
      <p>The most time-consuming step. Visit <a href="https://www.citapreviapolicia.es" target="_blank">cita previa policia.es</a> to book an appointment at your nearest National Police headquarters (Oficina de Policía Nacional). Waiting times vary significantly by location (2 weeks to 3+ months). Book as soon as possible.</p>

      <p><strong>Step 4: Attend Your Appointment</strong></p>
      <p>Arrive on time with all original documents and copies. The process typically takes 10-20 minutes. Have your passport ready, as the officer will verify your identity and ask why you need the NIE.</p>

      <p><strong>Step 5: Pay the Fee</strong></p>
      <p>The administrative fee is approximately €9.60 (can be paid in cash or card). This is the only cost associated with obtaining an NIE.</p>

      <p><strong>Step 6: Receive Your NIE Certificate</strong></p>
      <p>Upon completion, you'll receive an NIE certificate (Certificado de Asignación del NIE) with your assigned number. This certificate serves as official proof of your NIE and is required for opening bank accounts, buying property, and other administrative processes.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- DOCUMENTS REQUIRED -->
  <section class="msv__section msv__section--cream">
