        <h2>Documents Required</h2>
        <p>Everything you need to bring to your appointment</p>
      </div>
      <p><strong>Original Documents (must bring):</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Valid passport (EU citizens can use national ID cards)</li>
        <li>Completed form EX-15 (if not submitted online)</li>
        <li>Proof of address in Spain (rental contract, utilities bill, padron registration, or property deed)</li>
        <li>If representing someone else: power of attorney</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Copies to Bring:</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Passport: 2 photocopies (front and back)</li>
        <li>Proof of address: 1 photocopy</li>
        <li>All pages of form EX-15: 1 photocopy</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Optional but Helpful:</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Bank account information (if available)</li>
        <li>Copy of any Spanish visa or residence permit</li>
        <li>Print-out of your appointment confirmation (cita previa)</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="msv__alert msv__alert--warn">
        <span class="msv__alert-icon">⚠️</span>
        <p><strong>Proof of address requirements:</strong> You must have a Spanish address to obtain an NIE. If you haven't found accommodation yet, you can use a temporary address (hotel, Airbnb, friend's address). Some people successfully use a friend's address with written consent, though this varies by location.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

